How to Add Another Server Using the XML Updater
Purpose

Use the XML Updater section of the tool when you need to add a new server to an existing site entry, or create a new site entry with its assigned servers.

The XML Updater writes changes to the inventory XML file that the reporting tool uses to load sites, teams, and server lists.

Before You Start

Make sure you know the following information before adding a server:

Team Number
Example: 1, 2, 3, or 4
VISN
Example: V18
Site Abbreviation
Example: TVH
Team Name
Example: Blue, Red, Western, etc.
Server FQDN(s)
Example: IMMCR01.va.gov

Use the server’s full DNS name when possible.

Steps to Add Another Server
1. Open the application

Launch Clinical Imaging Admin Tools.

2. Go to the XML Updater section

From the left navigation menu, select XML Updater.

3. Enter the site information

Fill in the site fields exactly as they should exist in inventory:

Team Number
VISN
Site Abbreviation
Team Name

If you are adding a server to an existing site, these values must match the existing record.

4. Enter the server name

In the server field or server list area, add the new server’s FQDN.

If the updater accepts multiple servers, enter them in the expected format used by your tool version.

5. Run the update

Click the button used to submit the inventory update.

The tool will call the backend inventory update script and attempt to:

validate the entry
update the XML safely
preserve schema format
write the updated inventory file
6. Confirm success

Review the output or status message in the updater window.

A successful update should indicate the inventory change completed without validation errors.

Example
Example: Add a server to an existing site

If site TVH already exists under Team 1 and you want to add a new server:

Team Number: 1
VISN: V09
Site Abbreviation: TVH
Team Name: Blue
Server: IMMTCR03.va.gov

Then run the update
